# Cache policy for the static assets. Wrangler reads this file as configuration
# and does not upload it, the same way it treats .assetsignore.
#
# Cloudflare's default for Workers static assets is `max-age=0, must-revalidate`,
# which costs a conditional round-trip per file per page view. The walkthrough
# carousel alone is seven images totalling ~1.7 MB, so that default is the wrong
# trade here.
#
# Deliberately NOT `immutable`: these filenames are stable across regenerations
# (tools/rasterize-pdf.swift writes og-card.png in place, and the walkthrough
# slides are regenerated from Walkthrough_Slides_Clean.pdf under the same
# numbers), so an immutable response would strand returning visitors on an old
# image with no way to recover. A day of freshness plus a week of
# serve-stale-while-revalidating gets nearly all the benefit and still heals.
#
# The rules below are written NOT to overlap. Matching rules are additive, not
# most-specific-wins: a `/*` block plus a per-file block emits BOTH Cache-Control
# values into one comma-joined header, which is malformed. Every asset must be
# matched by exactly one rule.

/tradevision/walkthrough/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/sources-tracker/*
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

/professional-bio.pdf
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=86400, stale-while-revalidate=604800

# The link-preview card. Crawlers refetch on their own schedule and a wrong card
# is more visible than a slightly stale one, so keep this shorter than the rest.
/tradevision/og-card.png
  Cache-Control: public, max-age=3600, stale-while-revalidate=86400
